    <bpmn:process id="W_W1211" name="W1211. Store-Level Vendor &amp; Delivery Driver Access Control &amp; Yard Security Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor delivery truck arrives at store receiving dock; or 3PL driver arrives for customer delivery pickup; or service contractor arrives for maintenance
Frequency: 2–3 vendor deliveries per store per day + 3PL driver visits + occasional service contractors = ~5–8 external personnel access events per store per day
Volume: ~1,000–1,600 external access events per day chain-wide (200 stores × 5–8)
Owner: Receiving Clerk / LP Officer
Participants: Receiving Clerk, LP Officer, Vendor Driver, Store Manager, Security Guard
Source: workflow W1211 — Store-Level Vendor &amp; Delivery Driver Access Control &amp; Yard Security Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1211_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1211_Lane1" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1211_Lane2" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1211_Lane3" name="LP Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1211_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1211_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1211_Start6" name="Vendor delivery truck arrives at store receiving dock; or 3PL driver arrives for customer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task7" name="External personnel (vendor driver, 3PL driver, service contractor) arrives at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: External personnel (vendor driver, 3PL driver, service contractor) arrives at store entrance or receiving gate; Security Guard greets and requests: (a) government-issued ID, (b) delivery documents (DR, PO reference) or service work order, (c) vehicle plate number and details
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task8" name="Security Guard verifies identity and purpose: (a) checks delivery documents…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Security Guard verifies identity and purpose: (a) checks delivery documents against expected deliveries in system (Receiving Clerk&#x27;s daily delivery schedule from W109), (b) for service contractors: verifies against approved contractor list per W600, (c) for unexpected/unlisted deliveries: contacts Receiving Clerk for authorization
Responsible (R): Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1211_Task9" name="Security Guard logs visitor in access control system: (a) visitor name…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Security Guard logs visitor in access control system: (a) visitor name, company, ID number, vehicle plate, purpose, time-in, assigned escort; (b) issues color-coded visitor badge (green = vendor delivery, yellow = 3PL driver, orange = service contractor) with time-limited validity (max 2 hours for deliveries; max 8 hours for contractors); (c) retains visitor&#x27;s government ID at guard station
Responsible (R): Security Guard / System
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task10" name="Receiving Clerk receives notification and escorts vendor driver to receiving…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Receiving Clerk receives notification and escorts vendor driver to receiving dock; Receiving Clerk remains present throughout unloading; driver is NOT permitted in: (a) sales floor, (b) cash office, (c) stockroom beyond receiving staging area, (d) IT/server area
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: Duration of unloading</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task11" name="For lumber yard / outdoor materials deliveries: Security Guard or LP Officer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For lumber yard / outdoor materials deliveries: Security Guard or LP Officer monitors via CCTV; driver must remain within designated unloading zone; yard gate closed after entry
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Duration of unloading</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task12" name="Upon completion: Receiving Clerk verifies delivered goods match DR (W109 goods…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Upon completion: Receiving Clerk verifies delivered goods match DR (W109 goods receipt); signs delivery receipt; escorts driver back to exit; Security Guard checks: (a) vehicle cargo area visually inspected for unauthorized merchandise, (b) driver returns visitor badge, (c) Security Guard returns government ID, (d) logs time-out in access control system
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Security Guard
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1211_Task13" name="If visitor badge not returned within validity period: system alerts LP Officer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If visitor badge not returned within validity period: system alerts LP Officer; LP Officer locates visitor; if visitor cannot be located: Store Manager notified; LP Officer reviews CCTV footage for visitor&#x27;s last known location
Responsible (R): System / LP Officer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1211_Task14" name="Weekly: LP Officer reviews access control log for anomalies: (a) visitors…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: LP Officer reviews access control log for anomalies: (a) visitors exceeding time limit, (b) frequent visits by same vendor driver outside scheduled deliveries, (c) vehicles without proper documentation, (d) after-hours access events; escalates patterns to LP Director
Responsible (R): LP Officer
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1211_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1211_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1211_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1211_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-311 (ensure controlled execution — Physical Security &amp; Surveillance (PA-23.2).) | - operational: Receiving Clerk / LP Officer review and approval gate
Owner: Receiving Clerk / LP Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
