    <bpmn:process id="W_W1388" name="W1388. Store CCTV System Daily Health Check, Footage Retention &amp; Incident Retrieval Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — daily (automated health check); ad-hoc (incident investigation request from W37 or W562)
Frequency: Daily automated health check; ~10–20 incident footage retrieval requests/week chain-wide
Volume: 200 stores × ~32 cameras/store = ~6,400 cameras; ~15 TB of footage generated daily chain-wide
Owner: Loss Prevention Analyst (LP Operations Center)
Participants: LP Analyst, LPO (Loss Prevention Officer), Store Manager, HR (for employee investigations), Legal (for police reports)
Source: workflow W1388 — Store CCTV System Daily Health Check, Footage Retention &amp; Incident Retrieval Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1388_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1388_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1388_Lane2" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1388_Lane3" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1388_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1388_Start5" name="Scheduled — daily (automated health check); ad-hoc (incident investigation request from…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1388_Task6" name="Automated daily health check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated daily health check (4:00 AM): system checks all cameras per store — (a) camera online/offline status, (b) recording active (NVR writing footage), (c) storage capacity (days of footage remaining at current resolution), (d) image quality (blur, darkness, obstruction detection via AI); generates health report with exception list of cameras requiring attention
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): LP Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1388_Task7" name="LP Analyst reviews health report at start of shift: (a) offline cameras —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: LP Analyst reviews health report at start of shift: (a) offline cameras — identify root cause (power outage, network failure, hardware malfunction); dispatch Facilities Technician for on-site repair if needed; (b) storage capacity warnings — initiate archival or increase storage; (c) image quality issues — dispatch cleaning (lens) or repositioning; (d) for cameras covering high-risk areas (POS, high-value merchandise, receiving dock) — priority repair SLA: 4 hours (same day)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1388_Task8" name="Footage retention management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Footage retention management: system enforces retention policy per camera type: (a) POS cameras and high-value area cameras: 90 days; (b) entrance/exit and parking lot cameras: 60 days; (c) receiving dock cameras: 90 days; (d) general store floor cameras: 30 days; (e) footage related to open investigations (flagged with hold code): retained until investigation closed + 1 year; (f) footage related to legal proceedings (litigation hold): retained until Legal releases hold; (g) system auto-deletes footage past retention period unless hold code applied
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): LP Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1388_Task9" name="Incident footage retrieval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Incident footage retrieval: when LPO or Store Manager requests footage for an investigation: (a) requestor submits footage request via LP ticketing system: store, camera, date/time range, incident description, urgency (standard 24 hours or urgent 2 hours); (b) LP Analyst retrieves footage from NVR (remote access for most stores); (c) clips relevant segment; (d) saves to evidence vault (secured network storage with restricted access); (e) applies retention hold code; (f) notifies requestor of footage availability
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1388_Task10" name="Data privacy compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data privacy compliance: all CCTV footage access is logged — who accessed, when, which camera, reason; LP Manager reviews access logs monthly; unauthorized access (e.g., viewing footage for non-business reasons) is a policy violation subject to disciplinary action; footage is not shared externally (police, third parties) without Legal approval and data privacy impact assessment per RA 10173
Responsible (R): LP Manager
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1388_Task11" name="Monthly system performance report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly system performance report: LP Analyst generates monthly CCTV health report — (a) camera uptime % by store and region, (b) offline incidents and resolution time, (c) storage utilization trend, (d) footage retrieval request volume and SLA compliance, (e) cameras reaching end-of-life for replacement planning
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1388_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1388_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1388_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1388_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-311 (ensure controlled execution — Physical Security &amp; Surveillance (PA-23.2).) | - operational: Loss Prevention Analyst (LP Operations Center) review and approval gate
Owner: Loss Prevention Analyst (LP Operations Center)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1388_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1388_Annotation13" targetRef="W1388_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
