    <bpmn:process id="W_W1477" name="W1477. Key &amp; Access Credential Management, Master Key System &amp; Store Lock Rotation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening; employee role change requiring access modification; key/credential loss; employee termination; or periodic security review
Frequency: Per access change request (~50–100/month chain-wide); semi-annual key audit; lock rotation per schedule
Volume: 200 stores × ~15–20 keys/access points per store = ~3,000–4,000 managed keys; ~6,925 employee access credentials
Owner: LP Operations Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Facilities Coordinator, IT Security, HR (employee status changes), Locksmith Vendor
Source: workflow W1477 — Key &amp; Access Credential Management, Master Key System &amp; Store Lock Rotation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1477_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1477_Lane1" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1477_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1477_Lane3" name="Facilities Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1477_Lane4" name="LP Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1477_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1477_Start6" name="New store opening; employee role change requiring access modification; key/credential…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task7" name="Access provisioning for new employees">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Access provisioning for new employees: (a) during onboarding per W19.1: HR system triggers access provisioning request to LP Operations; (b) LP Operations configures access credential based on role: (i) Store Manager: all areas, (ii) Department Supervisor: sales floor, backroom, receiving dock, (iii) Cashier: sales floor, cash office (during shift only), (iv) Stock Associate: sales floor, backroom, receiving dock, lumber yard, (v) Maintenance/Utility: all areas except cash office, (vi) CSR: sales floor, customer service counter; (c) system creates access profile linked to employee ID; (d) employee receives RFID badge and store key(s) based on role; (e) employee signs key receipt acknowledging responsibility and return obligation
Responsible (R): HR / LP Operations
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task8" name="Access modification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Access modification: (a) when employee role changes (e.g., Sales Associate promoted to Department Supervisor): Store Manager submits access change request; (b) LP Operations updates access profile: add new areas, remove areas no longer needed; (c) if additional physical keys required: issue and document; if keys to be returned: collect and document; (d) system logs all access changes with timestamp and authorizer
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP Operations
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 10 min/change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task9" name="Access revocation on separation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Access revocation on separation: (a) when employee separates (resignation, termination) per W19.5: HR system triggers access revocation; (b) LP Operations revokes access: (i) deactivate RFID badge in system immediately (within 1 hour of separation notification), (ii) collect all physical keys from employee at exit, (iii) for involuntary terminations (theft, policy violation): Store Manager ensures employee is escorted out and keys collected before employee leaves premises; (c) if keys not returned: (i) document as &quot;Key Not Returned&quot; in security incident log, (ii) assess risk level based on key type (master key = critical, individual door key = moderate), (iii) for critical keys: schedule lock change within 48 hours per step 5
Responsible (R): HR / LP Operations / Store Manager
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 15 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task10" name="Semi-annual key audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Semi-annual key audit: (a) Store Manager conducts semi-annual key audit: (i) verify all issued keys are accounted for (physical count against key issuance log), (ii) verify all employee access credentials match current active employees (no separated employees with active badges), (iii) check key storage: are master keys secured in locked key cabinet with limited access? (iv) verify spare key inventory is complete and secured; (b) report discrepancies to LP Operations Manager: (i) keys not accounted for — investigate (lost? stolen? employee forgot to return?), (ii) access credentials for separated employees still active — immediate revocation; (c) audit results filed with LP case management system
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 1 hour/store (semi-annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task11" name="Lock rotation &amp; rekeying">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Lock rotation &amp; rekeying: (a) scheduled lock rotation: high-security locks (cash office, IT closet, chemical storage) rekeyed every 2 years; standard locks (backroom, receiving dock) rekeyed every 3 years; (b) emergency rekeying: triggered by (i) master key not returned by terminated employee (within 48 hours), (ii) confirmed key duplication (discovery of unauthorized copy), (iii) burglary or attempted break-in per W1389; (c) Facilities Coordinator engages locksmith vendor for rekeying: (i) new keys issued and documented per step 1, (ii) old keys collected and destroyed, (iii) system updated with new key code
Responsible (R): Facilities Coordinator / LP Operations
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1477_Task12" name="Master key system governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Master key system governance: (a) LP Operations Manager maintains BuildRight master key system hierarchy: (i) Grand Master Key (GMK) — opens all locks in all stores (held by COO and LP Operations Manager only, stored in HQ safe), (ii) Store Master Key (SMK) — opens all locks in one store (held by Store Manager and ASM, stored in store safe), (iii) Sub-Master Key — opens specific zone (receiving area, cash office), (iv) Individual Key — opens single door; (b) policy: no employee holds keys above their authorization level; master key duplication requires LP Operations Manager written authorization; (c) annual: LP Operations Manager reviews master key system integrity with locksmith vendor
Responsible (R): LP Operations Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1477_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1477_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1477_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1477_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-311 (ensure controlled execution — Physical Security &amp; Surveillance (PA-23.2).) | - operational: automated HR→LP system trigger; operational: trigger; operational: strict custody (HQ safe, two-person access) and emergency rekeying protocol
Owner: LP Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1477_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1477_Annotation14" targetRef="W1477_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1477_Flow16" sourceRef="W1477_Start6" targetRef="W1477_Task7" />
