    <bpmn:process id="W_W1478" name="W1478. DC Perimeter Security, Gate Access Control &amp; Visitor Management System" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily DC operations (gate access management); visitor arrival; contractor/service provider access; or security incident at DC perimeter
Frequency: Daily — ~100–150 vehicle entries/exits per DC per day; ~20–30 visitor entries per DC per day; quarterly perimeter security audit
Volume: 4 DCs × ~150 vehicle movements/day = ~600 vehicle movements/day; ~80–120 visitors/day across all DCs
Owner: DC Manager
Participants: DC Security Guard, DC Receiving Supervisor, Warehouse Supervisor, DC Manager, LP Operations (audit), Visitor/Vendor/Contractor
Source: workflow W1478 — DC Perimeter Security, Gate Access Control &amp; Visitor Management System</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1478_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1478_Lane1" name="Security Guard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1478_Lane2" name="LP Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1478_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1478_Start4" name="Daily DC operations (gate access management); visitor arrival; contractor/service…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1478_Task5" name="Employee gate access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Employee gate access: (a) DC employees badge in at the gate using RFID badge per W19.3 time &amp; attendance — system verifies: (i) employee is active (not separated), (ii) employee is assigned to this DC, (iii) access is within authorized hours; (b) security guard visually verifies badge photo matches person; (c) for employees arriving outside normal shift hours: security guard contacts DC Receiving Supervisor or Warehouse Supervisor for authorization before allowing entry
Responsible (R): Security Guard / System
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: Per entry (automated + visual check)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1478_Task6" name="Vehicle gate access — delivery &amp; vendor trucks">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vehicle gate access — delivery &amp; vendor trucks: (a) truck arrives at DC gate: driver presents delivery appointment reference (scheduled via W3 or W4); (b) system verifies appointment: (i) is there a scheduled inbound or outbound shipment for this vendor/carrier? (ii) is the expected vehicle plate number matching? (iii) is the driver name on the approved driver list for this carrier? (c) if verified: security guard issues visitor badge and records: driver name, company, vehicle plate, purpose (inbound delivery, outbound pickup, vendor visit), expected duration, time in; (d) if not verified: security guard contacts DC Receiving Supervisor to confirm or deny entry; (e) truck proceeds to designated dock door per receiving schedule; (f) upon departure: security guard verifies truck has been released by DC Receiving Supervisor (no unauthorized cargo), records time out, collects visitor badge
Responsible (R): Security Guard / DC Receiving Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 5 min/vehicle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1478_Task7" name="Visitor &amp; contractor access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Visitor &amp; contractor access: (a) visitor arrives: security guard verifies visit authorization: (i) pre-registered in visitor management system by DC host employee, or (ii) walk-in visitor with legitimate business purpose — host employee must confirm; (b) visitor logs in: name, company, purpose, host employee, time in; (c) security guard issues visitor badge (color-coded: yellow for office visitors, orange for warehouse floor access — requires host escort); (d) visitor must be escorted at all times in warehouse areas; (e) for contractors (maintenance, IT, construction): (i) contractor presents work order or service ticket, (ii) DC Manager or designee approves access, (iii) contractor completes safety induction (2 min — emergency exits, PPE requirements, restricted areas), (iv) contractor badge limited to authorized work area only
Responsible (R): Security Guard / DC Manager
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/visitor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1478_Task8" name="Perimeter patrol &amp; incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Perimeter patrol &amp; incident response: (a) security guard conducts perimeter patrol every 2 hours (24/7): (i) check fence/wall integrity, (ii) check all gates locked, (iii) check exterior lighting operational, (iv) check CCTV cameras per W838 operational and not obstructed, (v) check fire exits clear and alarmed; (b) any perimeter breach (cut fence, forced gate, unauthorized person on property): security guard activates incident response per W1389 protocol — contact PNP, DC Manager, LP Operations; (c) DC Manager reviews daily security log: entries, exits, incidents, patrol findings
Responsible (R): Security Guard / DC Manager
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 20 min/patrol (every 2 hours)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1478_Task9" name="Quarterly perimeter security audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly perimeter security audit: (a) LP Operations Manager audits each DC quarterly (rotating — one DC/month): (i) review visitor management records — are all visitors properly logged and badged? (ii) review vehicle access logs — are all trucks verified against appointments? (iii) physical inspection: fence condition, gate locks, CCTV coverage (no blind spots), lighting adequacy, fire exit integrity, forklift area barriers; (iv) test access controls: attempt entry without badge, attempt to tailgate, attempt to enter restricted area with wrong-color badge; (b) audit findings reported to DC Manager with remediation actions and deadlines; (c) COO reviews audit summary quarterly
Responsible (R): LP Operations Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day/DC/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1478_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1478_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1478_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1478_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-311 (ensure controlled execution — Physical Security &amp; Surveillance (PA-23.2).) | - operational: turnstile or mantrap at pedestrian entrance; operational: rather than relying on name recognition
Owner: DC Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1478_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1478_Annotation11" targetRef="W1478_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow13" sourceRef="W1478_Start4" targetRef="W1478_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow14" sourceRef="W1478_Task5" targetRef="W1478_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow15" sourceRef="W1478_Task6" targetRef="W1478_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow16" sourceRef="W1478_Task7" targetRef="W1478_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow17" sourceRef="W1478_Task8" targetRef="W1478_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1478_Flow18" sourceRef="W1478_Task9" targetRef="W1478_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1478_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1478_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1478">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_End10_di" bpmnElement="W1478_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1478_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1478_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W1478_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5534" name="W5534. Company-Property Gate Pass &amp; Asset-Exit Control (Stores, DCs &amp; HQ)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Any company asset or property crossing a premises exit — equipment dispatched for off-site repair (W5088/W3237 vendor service), inter-site equipment &amp; fixture transfers (store openings W16, remodels W226/W109), IT-asset redeployments (W3235-class), sold bulky goods released for customer pickup or delivery staging (W773/W1193), asset disposal &amp; e-waste removal (W3239), vendor/contractor tools signed in and out, or an LP audit spot-check
Frequency: Per-movement event (100% of asset exits); monthly register reconciliation; quarterly LP audit sampling
Volume: ~8,000–12,000 gate-pass movements/year across ~205 stores, 4 DCs and HQ — repair dispatches ~2,500–3,500; inter-site transfers ~1,500–2,500; disposal/e-waste removals ~400–600; customer bulky releases ~3,000–4,500; vendor/contractor tool sign-outs ~500–800
Owner: LP Officer (Store-Level) / Security Operations Center (SOC) Lead
Participants: Store Manager, DC Security Supervisor, Facilities Coordinator, IT Asset Administrator, Fixed-Asset Accountant (W276-class disposals), Guard Force, Vendor service engineers, Installing contractors
Source: workflow W5534 — Company-Property Gate Pass &amp; Asset-Exit Control (Stores, DCs &amp; HQ)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5534_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5534_Lane1" name="Requesting Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5534_Lane2" name="Guard Force">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5534_Lane3" name="LP Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5534_Lane4" name="LPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5534_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5534_Start6" name="Any company asset or property crossing a premises exit — equipment dispatched for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task7" name="Pass request &amp; authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pass request &amp; authorization: the requesting manager raises the gate pass in the ERP — asset IDs/serials, quantities, destination, expected return date or one-way disposal/transfer flag; approvals per the W1732 authority matrix (department head + asset owner; LP countersign for high-value items)
Responsible (R): Requesting Manager
Accountable (A): LP Officer (Store-Level)
Duration: 5–10 min per pass</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task8" name="Verification &amp; pass issuance at exit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Verification &amp; pass issuance at exit: the guard verifies physical items against the pass line items (asset tags/serials, barcode-scan where tagged), confirms the disposition (repair-vendor pickup, customer release, disposal hauler, transfer), and issues the numbered pass; customer bulky releases tie to the paid invoice or will-call claim (W773/W1193) before release
Responsible (R): Guard Force
Accountable (A): Store Manager / DC Security Supervisor
Duration: 5–15 min per movement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task9" name="Return reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Return reconciliation: for returnable passes, the guard verifies re-entry within the validity window; overdue passes escalate automatically to the issuing manager and LP; the asset register (W276/W3239) confirms the asset&#x27;s location status on return
Responsible (R): Guard Force / LP Officer
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 5 min per return; escalation at T+2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task10" name="Disposal &amp; one-way control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Disposal &amp; one-way control: one-way passes require the underlying document references attached before release — e-waste disposal certificates (W3239), inter-site transfer documents, waste-hauler pickup manifests; the hauler releases only against the scheduled manifest
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Fixed-Asset Accountant
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 10–15 min per one-way pass</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task11" name="Register &amp; monthly reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Register &amp; monthly reconciliation: LP reconciles the pass register against asset-movement records monthly — repair-vendor returns due, transfers in transit, disposal completions; discrepancies open W839-class investigation cases and feed shrinkage analytics (W845)
Responsible (R): LP Officer
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: 8–12 h/month chain-wide</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5534_Task12" name="Audit &amp; analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Audit &amp; analytics: the quarterly LP compliance audit (the W1174 program) samples gate-pass coverage and completeness at 10–15 stores/quarter; KPIs — pass coverage %, overdue-return %, discrepancy rate — report into the shrinkage-reduction program (W845) and the W1174 scoring
Responsible (R): LPO
Accountable (A): LP Officer
Duration: rides the W1174 audit cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5534_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5534_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
